Description: AstraOS installer configuration
 The Calamares configuration and branding that make the upstream Calamares installer
 an AstraOS installer: the module sequence, the partitioning defaults, the user
 creation policy, the summary and the AstraOS visual identity.
 .
 AstraOS does NOT ship a custom partitioning program and does not reimplement disk
 handling. Calamares performs all partitioning through kpmcore, which is the same
 path every distribution using Calamares takes (plan §10.1 and Rule 9: never
 compromise disk safety for convenience).
 .
 Safety properties enforced by this configuration:
  * the target disk is shown explicitly and is never assumed;
  * erasing a disk requires an explicit confirmation step;
  * no disk is formatted without user confirmation;
  * no fixed, shared or automatic login credentials are shipped;
  * installation can only be started by the user, never by a script.
