Description: AstraOS Windows command bridge
 The bridge for people arriving from Windows. It puts a set of familiar Windows
 commands on the PATH — dir, cls, copy, move, del, ren, md, rd, type, ipconfig,
 tasklist, taskkill, ping, tracert, netstat, sfc, chkdsk, shutdown and more — and
 maps each one onto the real Linux tool underneath, translating Windows switches
 (/y, /s, /t 0) and Windows-style paths as it goes.
 .
 Nothing here replaces a system component. Every command is a small entry point
 that calls /usr/lib/astraos/winbin/bridge, which executes the genuine Linux
 equivalent and prints a one-line hint the first time it differs in behaviour.
 'del' moves files to the trash (gvfs) instead of unlinking them, which is the
 Recycle-Bin behaviour a new user expects.
 .
 Also ships:
 .
  * astra(1)             one friendly front end for apt, system health and help
  * command_not_found_handle  names the Linux equivalent when a Windows command
                          that is not wrapped is typed
  * winmap(5) data       the single Windows-to-Linux mapping table behind the
                          bridge, 'astra help' and the shell suggestions
 .
 The wrappers are placed on the PATH through /etc/profile.d and the X11 session
 environment, never by shipping files into /usr/bin, so no package that owns a
 Linux command of the same name (coreutils' dir, net-tools' netstat) is ever
 overlapped at the dpkg level.
